-       A value is digested whole; `checksum` digests what is *behind* a value (a stream's
-       chunks, a file's content) without holding it, and `Digester` digests several values into
-       one accumulator. Without a permit, the compile error reads _this operation uses a
-       sub-optimal algorithm, key length or mode — or a checksum in place of a hash; import the
-       matching permit …_; without a provider it names the missing `Hash in algorithm`.
+       Un valor se resume entero; `checksum` resume lo que hay *detrás* de un valor (los
+       fragmentos de un flujo, el contenido de un fichero) sin retenerlo, y `Digester` resume
+       varios valores en un solo acumulador. Sin un permiso, el error de compilación dice _this
+       operation uses a sub-optimal algorithm, key length or mode — or a checksum in place of a
+       hash; import the matching permit …_; sin un proveedor, nombra el `Hash in algorithm` que
+       falta.

