-   entry .Acceptable   no weakness at all: SHA-2, BLAKE3, AES-GCM; its permit is always in scope
-   entry .Md5   digesting with MD5; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto` and `permitCryptoThrough2014` onward
-   entry .Sha1   digesting with SHA-1; granted by `permitDeprecatedCrypto`, `permitDisallowedCrypto`, `permitCryptoThrough2030`
-   entry .NonCryptographic   digesting with CRC-32, CRC-64, Adler-32 or MurmurHash3; granted by `permitNonCryptographicHashes`
-       Not a defect in the algorithm — a checksum does exactly what it claims — but a
-       concession that no adversary is in the threat model, since none of these resists a
-       deliberate collision.
-   entry .Tls10   accepting TLS 1.0; granted by `permitLegacyTls`
-   entry .Tls11   accepting TLS 1.1; granted by `permitLegacyTls`
-   entry .SmallDh   accepting ephemeral Diffie-Hellman shorter than 2048 bits; granted by `permitLegacyTls`
-   entry .CbcCipher   accepting CBC-mode TLS cipher suites; granted by `permitLegacyTls`
-   entry .ExpiredCertificate   accepting an expired peer certificate; granted by `permitUntrustedCertificates`
-   entry .SelfSignedCertificate   accepting a self-signed peer certificate; granted by `permitUntrustedCertificates`
-   entry .UnverifiedHostname   accepting a certificate whose name does not match the host; granted by `permitUntrustedCertificates`
-   entry .UncheckedRevocation   connecting without checking certificate revocation; granted by `permitUncheckedRevocation`
-   entry .Des   DES; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto` and `permitCryptoThrough2014` onward
-   entry .TripleDes   Triple-DES; applied under `permitDeprecatedCrypto`, processed under `permitLegacyCrypto`
-   entry .Rc2   RC2; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto` and `permitCryptoThrough2014` onward
-   entry .Blowfish   Blowfish; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto` and `permitCryptoThrough2014` onward
-   entry .SmallRsa   RSA with a key shorter than 2048 bits; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto`, `permitCryptoThrough2014` onward
-   entry .Dsa   DSA signatures; applied under `permitDisallowedCrypto`, processed under `permitLegacyCrypto`
-   entry .Ecb   ECB mode; granted by `permitDisallowedCrypto` only
-   entry .Unauthenticated   any unauthenticated (non-AEAD) cipher mode; granted by `permitUnauthenticatedCrypto`
+   entry .Acceptable   ninguna debilidad en absoluto: SHA-2, BLAKE3, AES-GCM; su permiso está siempre en el ámbito
+   entry .Md5   resumir con MD5; lo conceden `permitDisallowedCrypto` y `permitCryptoThrough2014` en adelante
+   entry .Sha1   resumir con SHA-1; lo conceden `permitDeprecatedCrypto`, `permitDisallowedCrypto`, `permitCryptoThrough2030`
+   entry .NonCryptographic   resumir con CRC-32, CRC-64, Adler-32 o MurmurHash3; lo concede `permitNonCryptographicHashes`
+       No es un defecto del algoritmo —una suma de verificación hace exactamente lo que dice—,
+       sino una concesión de que no hay ningún adversario en el modelo de amenazas, ya que ninguno
+       de ellos resiste una colisión deliberada.
+   entry .Tls10   aceptar TLS 1.0; lo concede `permitLegacyTls`
+   entry .Tls11   aceptar TLS 1.1; lo concede `permitLegacyTls`
+   entry .SmallDh   aceptar Diffie-Hellman efímero de menos de 2048 bits; lo concede `permitLegacyTls`
+   entry .CbcCipher   aceptar suites de cifrado TLS en modo CBC; lo concede `permitLegacyTls`
+   entry .ExpiredCertificate   aceptar un certificado caducado del par; lo concede `permitUntrustedCertificates`
+   entry .SelfSignedCertificate   aceptar un certificado autofirmado del par; lo concede `permitUntrustedCertificates`
+   entry .UnverifiedHostname   aceptar un certificado cuyo nombre no coincide con el host; lo concede `permitUntrustedCertificates`
+   entry .UncheckedRevocation   conectar sin comprobar la revocación de certificados; lo concede `permitUncheckedRevocation`
+   entry .Des   DES; lo conceden `permitDisallowedCrypto` y `permitCryptoThrough2014` en adelante
+   entry .TripleDes   Triple-DES; se aplica bajo `permitDeprecatedCrypto`, se procesa bajo `permitLegacyCrypto`
+   entry .Rc2   RC2; lo conceden `permitDisallowedCrypto` y `permitCryptoThrough2014` en adelante
+   entry .Blowfish   Blowfish; lo conceden `permitDisallowedCrypto` y `permitCryptoThrough2014` en adelante
+   entry .SmallRsa   RSA con una clave de menos de 2048 bits; lo conceden `permitDisallowedCrypto`, `permitCryptoThrough2014` en adelante
+   entry .Dsa   firmas DSA; se aplica bajo `permitDisallowedCrypto`, se procesa bajo `permitLegacyCrypto`
+   entry .Ecb   modo ECB; lo concede solo `permitDisallowedCrypto`
+   entry .Unauthenticated   cualquier modo de cifrado no autenticado (no AEAD); lo concede `permitUnauthenticatedCrypto`

- entry .Signing   what a signing algorithm does: sign bytes with a private key, verify with a public one
+ entry .Signing   lo que hace un algoritmo de firma: firmar bytes con una clave privada, verificar con una pública

= entry .Signing   what a signing algorithm does: sign bytes with a private key, verify with a public one
-   detail
+   detail

-       The interface enigmatic's asymmetric ciphers (`Rsa`, `Ecdsa`) and its HMAC adapter
-       implement, declared here so that a library below enigmatic can take "something which
-       signs" as a value. Keys and signatures are raw `Data`; enigmatic's `PrivateKey#sign` and
-       `PublicKey#verify` are the typed, permit-gated front to it.
-   entry #sign   the signature of `data` under `privateKey`, as bytes
-   entry #verify   whether `signature` is `data`'s signature under `publicKey`
+       La interfaz que implementan los cifrados asimétricos de enigmatic (`Rsa`, `Ecdsa`) y su
+       adaptador HMAC, declarada aquí para que una biblioteca por debajo de enigmatic pueda tomar
+       «algo que firma» como valor. Las claves y las firmas son `Data` en bruto; `PrivateKey#sign`
+       y `PublicKey#verify` de enigmatic son su fachada tipada y protegida por permisos.
+   entry #sign   la firma de `data` con `privateKey`, como bytes
+   entry #verify   si `signature` es la firma de `data` con `publicKey`

